#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110374 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dee17b1d-686f-5817-b7dd-bf5b0bbd3da3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Segments on a Number Line"}] :question/id #uuid "8d23b33d-46ad-56af-853c-353c306c7af0" :question/math-academy-id "e-2553" :question/problem "![](images/8b/8bc5a70179a245c26f766e7c0efb36b508d259746a6a92b02c4d423d39940d5a.png)\n\n  \n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AC=BD$\n\nII. $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$\n\nIII. $\\overline{AB}$ is congruent to $\\overline{BD}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that $AC= BD=5$ units.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $AB=CD=3$ units, we have that $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$.\n\n- Statement III is false since $AB=3$, while $BD = 5.$ So, $\\overline{AB}\\ncong \\overline{BD}$.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110375 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb023488-e5ec-5d04-9cc2-b40db799887c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Line Segments on a Grid"}] :question/id #uuid "a53bc0ac-2deb-53f9-a4cf-2ac02b903cd2" :question/math-academy-id "e-2554" :question/problem "Which of the line segments shown below are congruent?\n\n![](images/fe/fea89643ee848c5cce4ea9844da71fae26f4799c4dbbe5795086a5365fbf3ec9.png)" :question/worked-solution "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB = 3$ units\n\n- $CD=EF = 4$ units\n\n- $GH = 2$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent line segments is $\\overline{CD}\\cong\\overline{EF}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69275189-af69-51ce-bfc0-5f03976c117f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Line Segments on a Given Plane Figure"}] :question/id #uuid "e5cdb5e0-0ea7-5a96-81d4-0b53e2ad2f9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-2556" :question/problem "For the diagram shown below, which of the following statements are true? \n\n![](images/79/793dacde520b1be4aa4a1e023760a06d1db5fe23266ec1277efe948e8ca04ab1.png)\n\n \n\nI. The segments $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BE}$\n\nIII. $BE = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. In the picture, both $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have the same double hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BD}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, we can see that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BC}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BC} \\not\\cong \\overline{BE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the picture, we have that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BE} \\not\\cong \\overline{BD}.\n$$\n\nHence, ${BE} \\neq {BD},$ and since ${BD} = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$, we have $BE \\neq 4\\,\\textrm{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb023488-e5ec-5d04-9cc2-b40db799887c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Line Segments on a Grid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b55d9ad-d125-558a-81f9-5d73ea9169f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446497} {:answer/id #uuid "7f494db1-50d3-56cb-8e05-a1b5329875fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446507} {:answer/id #uuid "f054e55f-b130-59c9-9267-319c6a3272ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{EF}$ and $\\overset{―}{GH}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446530} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e0b450-c2c2-5523-8065-e4c2bcd6455c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{GH}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446532} {:answer/id #uuid "fef54bfa-f07f-59e8-bec9-bb54e349e1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{CD}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f494db1-50d3-56cb-8e05-a1b5329875fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446507} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5935cda-3ca0-5a2c-b098-daf654724f64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3965a7d-c65e-545a-bf90-c696ecfb9f09" :question/math-academy-id "q-113356" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4bfd5f3d064d03dc01603ba8af47bf2d75c2ec689c7068aa280b0f0ee95fbf3c.png)\n\nWhich of the line segments shown above are congruent?" :question/worked-solution "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB=EF=2$ units\n\n- $CD=3$ units\n\n- $GH=4$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent segments is $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dee17b1d-686f-5817-b7dd-bf5b0bbd3da3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Segments on a Number Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9dc503-0a07-5097-a04b-df1521025175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446494} {:answer/id #uuid "30fd724c-1e66-5545-910b-cba70b9ceccb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446498} {:answer/id #uuid "451f23a0-08b7-5bf9-9ecb-708cc75495d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446503} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8e6269-b588-5b3d-bd17-021aba4b8e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446513} {:answer/id #uuid "a58c6ae5-9720-5470-83a3-218cbbd67981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a58c6ae5-9720-5470-83a3-218cbbd67981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446515} :answer-field/id #uuid "71066348-df91-503c-b4df-3d488597f0dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76666e28-5611-55ce-b027-734929c0efa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-113378" :question/problem "![](images/00/001420c2d9eea57191ce6be891e503de29ea7919af3b84ccf2d0b559c985617d.png)\n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\overset{―}{BC}≅\\overset{―}{CD}$\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{CD}$\n\nIII. $\\overset{―}{AC}$ is congruent to $\\overset{―}{BD}$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. Indeed, we have that $BC=2$ units while $CD=3$ units. So, $\\overset{―}{BC}≇\\overset{―}{CD.}$\n\n- Statement II is true since $AB=CD=3$ units. So, $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{CD.}$\n\n- Statement III is true since $AC=BD=5.$ So, $\\overset{―}{AC}$ is congruent to $\\overset{―}{BD}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69275189-af69-51ce-bfc0-5f03976c117f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Line Segments on a Given Plane Figure"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14f3d1dd-b7aa-5606-92fa-8f606c3c8b23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446496} {:answer/id #uuid "3d450c53-59ff-5e26-a0e6-1963c8cdfb6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446500} {:answer/id #uuid "3d687982-8928-5334-9445-9070d362aff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446501} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7b8203-f2ab-52dc-b7ba-9d4290aef807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446502} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc4150d-fbd2-53f5-b2fa-3dada3fa54cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fc4150d-fbd2-53f5-b2fa-3dada3fa54cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446508} :answer-field/id #uuid "07dcff8a-6d6f-5747-8d24-af20d21d6344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90696491-f11a-5ce4-ba23-2e9e528653c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-113396" :question/problem "![](images/41/41d9a3bcc715c0d5db4a910906f471695455065d198d90f3fa6d540e8cdb1c03.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CD}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AE}≅\\overset{―}{AB}$\n\nIII. $BD=4\\,\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CD}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BC}≇\\overset{―}{CD}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{AE}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ have the same hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AE}≅\\overset{―}{AB}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. From the picture, the two $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BD}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≇\\overset{―}{BD}.\n$$\n\nHence, $AB\\ne BD,$ and since $AB=4\\,\\text{cm},$ we have $BD\\ne 4\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69275189-af69-51ce-bfc0-5f03976c117f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Line Segments on a Given Plane Figure"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "391d0816-5c4e-597f-9a2b-7df77f7a1c1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446499} {:answer/id #uuid "76c91554-4c9b-5305-a578-4304308c8366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446505} {:answer/id #uuid "d01bd079-4f5c-5514-8964-aa8fffcddd2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446522} {:answer/id #uuid "d376981d-dfa3-5241-9f4c-d896f3a735b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446523} {:answer/id #uuid "e53cdf86-8d72-5abb-a4c5-558ca2d86b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d01bd079-4f5c-5514-8964-aa8fffcddd2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446522} :answer-field/id #uuid "2116cc24-7323-512a-ae0d-02a9716f23ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbeab3a9-f2b6-54a4-9522-21b49d07ec48" :question/math-academy-id "q-113405" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a94a13b06d682fe525278b529ed862cbfacecc3a97900ad54a80d66bf4971658.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{DB}≅\\overset{―}{CE}$\n\nIII. $AD=2\\,\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≇\\overset{―}{BC}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{DB}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{DB}≇\\overset{―}{CE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ have the same hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AD}≅\\overset{―}{BC}.\n$$\n\nHence, $AD=BC=2\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69275189-af69-51ce-bfc0-5f03976c117f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Line Segments on a Given Plane Figure"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52e9998d-fbdc-5120-b6ec-5e57464f505c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446504} {:answer/id #uuid "8bbae0e2-1659-50b0-aa2a-1eef7525b6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446510} {:answer/id #uuid "95718bfd-f92e-5b92-af62-d2230c2d2b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446511} {:answer/id #uuid "e78b583d-9757-5be5-b19b-add75ac3445d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446525} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5e6fa3-e724-5eb0-9f5d-1f0fa004c3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee5e6fa3-e724-5eb0-9f5d-1f0fa004c3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446529} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f4e1a9b-a9d1-5524-bd07-0fc9b61f95e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bf86eb0-0d69-505c-9f67-1fb5751e701a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113406" :question/problem "![](images/63/63789e47ee7a429edd48100456e3c8fdb536a1f67542c27ef687e5e85553f899.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{AD}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AC}≅\\overset{―}{BC}$\n\nIII. $BE\\ne 4\\,\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{AD}$ have the same hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{AD}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ have the same double hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AC}≅\\overset{―}{BC}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BE}$ have the same hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{BE}.\n$$\n\nHence, $AB=BE=4\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69275189-af69-51ce-bfc0-5f03976c117f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Line Segments on a Given Plane Figure"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0538352e-c960-5edd-b769-4afa4dadefe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446492} {:answer/id #uuid "9a1a2615-71f9-59bf-853a-7afb1994c394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446512} {:answer/id #uuid "ba283659-1139-5029-b99b-fe2c124abc2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446519} {:answer/id #uuid "cb91ead7-c25d-576e-866d-536a9a359a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446521} {:answer/id #uuid "eab6eba6-033b-5909-b595-c87cbe2fed1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb91ead7-c25d-576e-866d-536a9a359a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446521} :answer-field/id #uuid "70f63dd8-03b3-522d-a3a2-f59eedc2c7d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51446c30-9b6a-505e-b4e5-79d8ad4dcdb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-113408" :question/problem "![](images/a5/a5373ce6d1ab92c8b71feccf545a79b2515b66198ec4ffb557c9501a171b8021.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ are congruent\n\nII. $DC=CE$\n\nIII. $BD=3\\,\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ have the same double hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BC}≅\\overset{―}{CE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{DC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{DC}≇\\overset{―}{CE}.\n$$\n\nHence, $DC\\ne CE.$\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the picture, we have that $\\overset{―}{BD}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ have the same hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BD}≅\\overset{―}{AB}.\n$$\n\nHence, $BD=AB=3\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb023488-e5ec-5d04-9cc2-b40db799887c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Line Segments on a Grid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd729ab-f613-5980-9ba5-673eb732d533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AC}$ and $\\overset{―}{FG}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446495} {:answer/id #uuid "86fb6e3b-88c4-5b82-8829-e1d84f39232a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{DE}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446509} {:answer/id #uuid "b3aba2ab-e0f7-5e7e-80b6-3dfd18376883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AC}$ and $\\overset{―}{DE}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446517} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1b7f3a-0e73-5a2b-aeeb-089eac72d427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{DE}$ and $\\overset{―}{FG}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446528} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d6c1e9-7036-5f27-af7a-fa25e18b0f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{AC}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d6c1e9-7036-5f27-af7a-fa25e18b0f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{AC}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446531} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7b37f3-57d0-50b2-816e-291734505112" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02b1f120-5924-58fd-afb2-36fdecec673f" :question/math-academy-id "q-52615" :question/problem "![](images/ed/ede04322d50034c955e6c954d99bfbfc1f13e7b7e40fd9eb12f660e995e018a0.png)\n\nWhich of the line segments shown above are congruent?" :question/worked-solution "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB=AC=4$ units\n\n- $DE=5$ units\n\n- $FG=6$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent segments is $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{AC}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dee17b1d-686f-5817-b7dd-bf5b0bbd3da3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Segments on a Number Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020499ba-78b6-5552-952e-1513094a7f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446491} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc897fb-074a-54a5-bc11-82ecd98b176c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446514} {:answer/id #uuid "e8452f70-f910-5391-b495-143107593373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446526} {:answer/id #uuid "f8473e0c-62b4-58e6-a483-42bfb6112feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446533} {:answer/id #uuid "f931f61d-4047-5139-aa5b-4543e487c8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "020499ba-78b6-5552-952e-1513094a7f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446491} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d1ab693-4d0d-59c5-a7d6-6ddbae4541c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8399cd2-30cf-5b56-a133-fda3fd7126cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-53129" :question/problem "![](images/10/101d333d2309238209b3e5ce96fdf2a6e6881e2577a2dfc0b0b0114419a938ad.png)\n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $PQ=QR$\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{PR}≅\\overset{―}{QS}$\n\nIII. $PR=RS$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true since $PQ=QR=20$ units.\n\n- Statement II is false since $PR=40$ units, while $QS=50$ units. So, $\\overset{―}{PR}≇\\overset{―}{QS}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, we have that $PR=40$ units, while $RS=30$ units. So, $PR\\ne RS.$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69275189-af69-51ce-bfc0-5f03976c117f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Line Segments on a Given Plane Figure"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0824ac96-69d8-5ebc-b715-d16735e64e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446493} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0d8977-aa92-5e84-a9ef-b749cedf76b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446506} {:answer/id #uuid "abc732d7-d392-5f07-8c26-e740fa66d1e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446516} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c35187-837a-5081-89a9-be725344a90e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446518} {:answer/id #uuid "babf8b40-36ce-53b6-922b-79925ab2ab44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abc732d7-d392-5f07-8c26-e740fa66d1e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446516} :answer-field/id #uuid "6095e7a0-db08-52d4-91d0-ee2e6637d22f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f0cab83-1e6c-56a1-bd89-cee806fa30d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-67597" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7f2467ce2b4c3e1a446b3fb50b88c77ad70db02293f7f8a8f76ba4bd718bebdb.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{DB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BE}$ are not congruent\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AD}≅\\overset{―}{BE}$\n\nIII. $CE\\ne 5\\,\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{DB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BE}$ have the same hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{DB}≅\\overset{―}{BE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the picture, we have that $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BE}$ have different hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AD}≇\\overset{―}{BE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the picture, we have that $\\overset{―}{BE}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ have different hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BE}≇\\overset{―}{CE}.\n$$\n\nHence, $BE\\ne CE,$ and since $BE=5\\,\\text{cm}$, we have $CE\\ne 5\\,\\text{cm}.$,\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}]}
